ñ{"text": "# Release Notes for v2.4.0\n\nThis release brings new features, performance improvements, bug fixes, and updated documentation. Below is a summary of changes grouped by type.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Add `--since` flag to export command**  \n  The `export` command now supports a `--since` flag, allowing users to filter results based on a timestamp or date. This is useful for incremental data exports.  \n  *(Contributed by dana, a1c3e5f)*\n\n- **Support YAML output format**  \n  In addition to existing formats, command output can now be exported in YAML format using the appropriate flag (e.g., `--format yaml`).  \n  *(Contributed by dana, c3e5a7b)*\n\n## Bug Fixes\n\n- **Handle empty config file without crashing**  \n  The application now gracefully handles cases where the configuration file exists but is empty, instead of raising a parsing error.  \n  *(Contributed by lee, b2d4f6a)*\n\n- **Correct timezone in log timestamps**  \n  Log entries now display timestamps in the correct local timezone, fixing an issue where UTC was incorrectly assumed.  \n  *(Contributed by lee, e5a7c9d)*\n\n- **Retry uploads on HTTP 503 errors**  \n  Failed uploads due to server-side temporary errors (HTTP 503) are now automatically retried, improving reliability in unstable network conditions.  \n  *(Contributed by kim, b8d0f2a)*\n\n## Performance Improvements\n\n- **Cache parsed templates between runs**  \n  Templates are now cached after parsing, reducing startup time and CPU usage during repeated executions.  \n  *(Contributed by kim, f6b8d0e)*\n\n## Documentation\n\n- **Document the plugin API**  \n  Comprehensive documentation for the plugin API has been added, enabling developers to extend functionality more easily.  \n  *(Contributed by sam, d4f6b8c)*\n\n## Miscellaneous\n\n- **Bump minimum Python version to 3.10**  \n  The minimum supported Python version is now 3.10. Users are encouraged to upgrade their environments accordingly.  \n  *(Contributed by sam, a7c9e1f)*\n\n